=== independent-review.md ===
# Independent review — inactive v2 authority verifier

Review base: GitHub main `a3ede65fedf45502eca2d845a0d46fbdd2d662b9`; repository bytes were independently grounded by the root agent before this review. Review scope is the new verifier, its protected parent/current contract, and independent compatibility/concurrent-call evidence. All existing application, SQL, parser, seal, bridge and policy files remain outside my editing scope.

## Sources reviewed

- `AGENTS.md` and latest `CONTINUE_HERE.md` completion block.
- `p5-voice-lifetime-change-contract-2026-11-02.md` in full, plus the new current-reader SQL in full.
- Preserved P3b `seal.server.ts`, legacy `voice-verification.server.ts`, `voice-admission.server.ts`, and `voice-store-adapter.server.ts`.
- Completed v2 issuer and parent/issuance, current, cleanup and proof transport interfaces/validation.
- New `voice-v2-authority-verifier.server.ts` implementation.

## Finding and verified correction

The first implementation ended its last protected current read with a final awaited Auth check, then returned evidence. Root identified that a same-identity Auth response could arrive after protected parent/current state changed during that final wait. I reproduced both cases: parent revocation and replacement of the exact approval digest in the fourth/final Auth callback. The expanded independent suite failed 2 of 7 cases, returning protocol-2 evidence in each case. This initial diagnostic is retained as `review-final-auth-initial.log`.

The corrected source performs a final protected parent/current recheck after that Auth wait, retaining the original query time, updated minimum identity expiry and original pinned immutable issuance/approval identity. Source review confirmed no later Auth wait follows that final protected snapshot. Both regressions now deny and the expanded suite passes 7/7 (`review-tests-confirmed.log`). This does not make Auth and SQL atomic; the final observation can also become stale, and all downstream transactions must independently revalidate. No finite read loop establishes durable admission or provider permission. No remaining implementation blocker was found in the bounded inactive verifier.

## Other review conclusions

- Each invocation owns its identity, parent version, original verification start, immutable issuance and approval identity, local monotonic time and minimum ceilings. The factory retains only captured methods, with no shared last-verified record or authority cache.
- The new strict own-data guard precedes the unchanged legacy parser. Accessors, symbol/extra fields and malformed nested data are denied rather than coerced. Local crypto uses the preserved AES-GCM/HMAC implementation; no mock crypto or fallback is installed.
- The first issuance lifetime is positive and at most 900000 ms, issued no later than original verification, and does not exceed the sealed envelope deadline. Its issuedAt/expiry remain exact across later observations, rather than rewriting immutable facts when Auth becomes shorter. Auth/allowlist/approval ceilings retain minima.
- Every current response carries and matches all nine query fields. Current thread/incarnation/revision and all nested owner/thread/attempt/fingerprint relationships are checked; parent version and actual Auth session remain fixed across waits.
- The result is detached frozen content-free protocol-2 evidence. It includes neither envelope nor private authority/writing/credentials; failures return null without raw causes. The unchanged legacy admission evidence schema rejects this result before any claim call, so no downgrade was introduced.
- `effectiveExpiresAt` includes the verification-age ceiling. This is conservative evidence freshness, not a new voice-session policy or permission to renew. Future orchestration must distinguish the retained original component lifetimes from proof freshness.

## Independent test coverage

New file: `src/lib/ai/conversation/__tests__/p5-voice-v2-authority-verifier-review.test.ts`.

