# Inactive v2 verifier implementation notes

Owned new files:
- `src/lib/ai/conversation/service/voice-v2-authority-verifier.server.ts`
- `src/lib/ai/conversation/__tests__/p5-voice-v2-authority-verifier.test.ts`

Separate server-only `createVoiceV2AuthorityVerifier` captures mandatory now/Auth/parent/current ports once. Each invocation has its own local timing, identity, association and shrink-only ceilings; no per-request state is retained by the factory. The five-field legacy request passes exact own-data/canonical-ID validation before the unchanged parser. Existing parser, P3b AES-GCM/HMAC, verifier and bridge files remain unchanged.

Conservative `verifiedAt` precedes initial Auth. All awaits are followed by safe monotonic local checks and strict original age <30000 ms. Same actual owner/session and exact parent/version remain pinned. Real unchanged unseal and keyed fingerprint operations authenticate the exact already-issued ciphertext. Full protocol-2 current receipts must echo all nine query fields. Thread/incarnation/revision, owner, fingerprint and exact approval ID/digest/attempt/scope match. Original issuance issuedAt/expiry remain immutable across reads, with a positive <=900000 interval, issuedAt no later than original verification, and issuance expiry no later than the envelope. Dynamic Auth/allowlist/approval ceilings can only shorten; current shorter Auth does not rewrite the original issuance.

Content-free frozen protocol-2 evidence includes original issuance and envelope deadlines, original verification/freshness ceiling and effective min deadline. It does not register proof/claim/cleanup, consume receipt, reserve quota, mark provider operation, return content, grant provider permission or infer permanent revocation. The protected current SQL may advance only its existing owner-clock high-water. Captured read-only ports do not install authentication/transport provenance; future host obligations and atomic downstream gates remain required.

Independent final-Auth regressions exposed an initial source gap: parent/approval could change during final Auth after the last protected snapshot. Corrected implementation finishes final Auth with protected same-parent and full current rechecks, followed only by local time validation. There is no subsequent Auth wait. Finite Auth/SQL observations still are not an atomic lock spanning systems or future eligibility.

Initial primary run: 87/88 pass. One malformed-input test used `.toUpperCase()` on an all-numeric UUID, so the UUID was unchanged and correctly reached Auth before failing crypto. Corrected fixture uses an actually uppercase alphabetic UUID; no assertion or source policy weakened. Expanded final parent/current coverage gives final primary 92/92 pass (`verifier-primary-corrected.log`).

Initial TypeScript ran while the SQL agent's new test was incomplete; only reported missing closing brace in that in-progress test. The diagnostic remains in `verifier-types-initial.log`. Completed-file TypeScript and scoped implementation/primary-test ESLint pass (`verifier-types-confirmed.log`, `verifier-lint.log`). Independent source review/7 cases and actual isolated SQL/45 cases are reported separately.

Primary fixture uses real local AES-GCM and keyed HMAC with a fictional test-only secret, explicit fictional request-bound Auth records and local current/clock doubles. It covers exact echo fields, late/expired/backward/unsafe timing, current associations, original issuance bounds and immutability, shortest observed deadlines, changed/revoked/foreign/legacy records, actual crypto tampering/wrong key/owner/thread/revision, malformed/accessor input, capture and privacy. Independent tests cover concurrent-call isolation and unchanged v1 bridge incompatibility. No deployed Auth, native concurrency, HTTP fault injection or provider/device evidence is claimed.

Final implementation and owned tests frozen after formatting, primary checks, TypeScript and scoped lint; root runs final aggregate checks once all files freeze.
